  // Wave directions (deg): 0° and 180° — each (Fn, λ/L) case is run for both.
  // With Fn=0.3 and this project’s RegularWave convention, 0° is following / stern-quartering
  // (cos β > 0) and 180° is head / bow-quartering (Region H in WaveForceRegion).
  // For 0° only, Fn=0.3 → U ≈ 5.146 m/s, cos β = 1:
  //   ω_c1 = g/(2U·cos β) ≈ 0.953 rad/s,  ω_c2 = g/(U·cos β) ≈ 1.906 rad/s
  // → ω_inc < ω_c1 : F1;  ω_c1 ≤ ω < ω_c2 : F2;  ω ≥ ω_c2 : F3.
  // The 15 λ/L values below span F1/F2/F3 at 0°; at 180° the solver uses the head-sea grid.
